# Visual and interaction design

<!-- LH-DESIGN-01 -->
Read AGENTS.md, applicable interface rules, the Spec, and existing design evidence. On entry, handoff, or resumption, use [Stage readiness and handoff](../lumine-plan/references/stage-handoff.md) to verify deliverables and user confirmation. Establish product direction in the Spec first; create design material after the user confirms entry into design. Product rules belong to lumine-plan, visual and interaction decisions to this Skill, and technical architecture design to the Plan. A review request produces judgment and evidence, not implementation by default.

<!-- LH-DESIGN-02 -->
Choose the smallest useful material for unresolved visual, interaction, or feasibility questions, such as an HTML prototype, flow diagram, or explanation. Reuse external designs, references, and approved approaches. Do not regenerate attachments merely because the work enters another stage or require DESIGN, component maps, and multiple handoff formats together.

<!-- LH-DESIGN-03 -->
Identify the pages/states covered, related Spec, and confirmation scope; iterate autonomously within design. Present reviewable deliverables and unresolved choices, then ask the user to confirm the design and proceed to supplement the Spec. Do not repeat a valid confirmation for the same deliverables. Document status and Agent judgment cannot replace confirmation, and earlier broad authorization cannot authorize an immediate move into technical planning or implementation.

<!-- LH-DESIGN-04 -->
Cover applicable normal, loading, empty, failed, unauthorized, cancelled, and recovery states. Review accessibility, narrow layouts, content density, and user-facing copy. Explain the objects, actions, and next steps users need, without development notes. Review alignment between product goals and visual/interaction decisions; deterministic checks cannot replace this judgment.

<!-- LH-DESIGN-05 -->
After the user confirms the design, use lumine-plan to supplement the same Spec with the resulting scenarios, behavior, rules, and acceptance, and link the material. For presentation-only details, update references and applicability without copying design prose. Present the supplemented Spec for confirmation before entering the Exec Plan; confirm the Plan before lumine-run. Do not hand design directly to implementation. Browser evidence after implementation is distinct from a design preview. Repo Wiki cards use text and HTML; do not generate card images with this Skill.

<!-- LH-DESIGN-06 -->
Use existing product, interaction, and interface knowledge or inspect implementation directly; a knowledge query is optional. Within authorization, preserve reusable implemented interface mechanisms and limits in Wiki. Unimplemented designs remain Spec attachments or Plan content.
